note A path is a tree, stored flat. Every step carries the index of the step it hangs under (None for a root; on disk, the parent's id) and nothing else; the tree shape is derived on demand, in pre-order, roots in list order and children in list order. That is what makes a flow readable top-down, and it is also why editing is cheap: appending a step is a push, deleting one moves its children up to its parent, and re-parenting is a single field plus a cycle check. Step indices are positions in the flat list and are what every command takes; they are never stored.

